  "id": "COMPOUND:16988 - PROTEIN:5829",
  "verbalization": "Indole-3-acetate is implicated in the biological pathway leading to CHP-134 through a series of interconnected targets. The evidence suggests that Indole-3-acetate acts as a target for Col2, which in turn is targeted by Belamcandal, and Belamcandal further targets CHP-134. This indicates a potential cascade of molecular interactions where Indole-3-acetate may influence the activity of Col2, which then modulates the function of Belamcandal, ultimately affecting CHP-134. The presence of multiple pathways converging on CHP-134 highlights the complexity of the regulatory network, with Indole-3-acetate serving as a central node in this interaction chain. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of Indole-3-acetate in orchestrating downstream effects that culminate in the action of CHP-134.",
